---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy – Talendos"
  description="Information about data processing on the Talendos website."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose legal">
      <p class="eyebrow">Data protection</p>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>

      <h2>1. Controller</h2>
      <p>
        Talendos GmbH<br />Richtstrecke 16a<br />45731 Waltrop<br />Germany
      </p>
      <p>
        Phone: <a href="tel:+4923099690200">+49 2309 9690200</a><br />
        Email: <a href="mailto:info@talendos.com">info@talendos.com</a>
      </p>

      <h2>2. Hosting and server logs</h2>
      <p>
        We host this static website using GitHub Pages, a service provided by
        GitHub, Inc., 88 Colin P. Kelly Jr. Street, San Francisco, CA 94107,
        USA. GitHub states that a visitor’s IP address is logged and stored for
        security purposes whenever a GitHub Pages website is accessed. In
        addition, technically necessary connection data such as the requested
        resource, date and time, browser information and referring page may be
        processed to deliver and secure the website.
      </p>
      <p>
        The legal basis for our use of GitHub Pages is Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR. Our
        legitimate interest is the secure, reliable and economical provision of
        this website. GitHub may process data in the United States and other
        countries. GitHub participates in the EU-US Data Privacy Framework and
        also refers to the European Commission’s standard contractual clauses
        for relevant international transfers. Details are available in the
        <a
          href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement"
          rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub Privacy Statement</a
        >. GitHub determines the retention of its security logs under its own
        policies. GitHub states that retention depends on the respective purpose
        and legal obligations, including security, dispute resolution and
        enforcement. We do not receive or maintain a separate visitor log.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Contact enquiries</h2>
      <p>
        If you contact us by email, telephone or fax, we process the information
        you provide to answer your enquiry and for possible follow-up questions.
        The legal basis is Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR where the request concerns a
        contract or pre-contractual measures; otherwise it is Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR,
        our legitimate interest in handling enquiries efficiently, or Art.
        6(1)(a) GDPR where consent is requested.
      </p>
      <p>
        We retain enquiry data only for as long as necessary for the purpose or
        as required by statutory retention obligations.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Cookies and analytics</h2>
      <p>
        The website code we provide does not set cookies or use analytics,
        advertising trackers, embedded third-party content or browser storage.
        All fonts and core assets are delivered from the same website origin. No
        cookies or browser-storage entries were observed during the live
        technical verification on 3 October 2026. Accordingly, no consent banner
        is required for the website in its current form.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Subject to the applicable legal requirements, you have rights to access,
        rectification, erasure, restriction of processing, data portability and
        objection. Where processing is based on consent, you may withdraw that
        consent at any time for the future. You also have the right to lodge a
        complaint with a competent data protection supervisory authority. The
        supervisory authority responsible for our registered office is the
        Landesbeauftragte für Datenschutz und Informationsfreiheit Nordrhein-
        Westfalen (LDI NRW), Kavalleriestraße 2–4, 40213 Düsseldorf, Germany, <a
          href="https://www.ldi.nrw.de/"
          rel="noopener noreferrer">www.ldi.nrw.de</a
        >.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Security</h2>
      <p>
        We use TLS encryption and appropriate technical and organisational
        measures to protect transmitted information. Internet communication can
        nevertheless not be guaranteed to be completely secure.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Status</h2>
      <p>Last updated: 3 October 2026.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  h1 {
    margin-block: 0.6rem 3rem;
  }
</style>
